# Unit25
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit25核心词汇

motive/ˈmoʊtɪv/动机/What was his motive for the crime?
narrative/ˈnærətɪv/叙述/The narrative of the novel is engaging.
neglect/nɪˈɡlekt/忽视/Don't neglect your health.
negotiate/nɪˈɡoʊʃieɪt/谈判/They are negotiating a deal.
neutral/ˈnjuːtrəl/中立的/Switzerland remained neutral.
nevertheless/ˌnevərðəˈles/然而/It was difficult; nevertheless, we succeeded.
norm/nɔːrm/规范/Social norms vary by culture.
notable/ˈnoʊtəbl/值得注意的/There has been notable improvement.
notion/ˈnoʊʃn/概念/The notion of equality is fundamental.
notorious/noʊˈtɔːriəs/臭名昭著的/The area is notorious for crime.
numerous/ˈnuːmərəs/众多的/Numerous studies support this theory.
objective/əbˈdʒektɪv/目标/Our main objective is quality.
obligation/ˌɑːblɪˈɡeɪʃn/义务/It is our obligation to protect the environment.
oblige/əˈblaɪdʒ/迫使/The law obliges companies to pay taxes.
obstacle/ˈɑːbstəkl/障碍/Lack of funding is a major obstacle.
occupation/ˌɑːkjuˈpeɪʃn/职业/What is your occupation?
offend/əˈfend/冒犯/I'm sorry if I offended you.
offense/əˈfens/冒犯/He was charged with a serious offense.
optimistic/ˌɑːptɪˈmɪstɪk/乐观的/She is optimistic about the future.
option/ˈɑːpʃn/选择/You have several options.
orient/ˈɔːrient/使适应/She oriented herself to the new environment.
outline/ˈaʊtlaɪn/轮廓/She gave a brief outline of the plan.
overall/ˌoʊvərˈɔːl/总体的/The overall quality is good.
overwhelming/ˌoʊvərˈwelmɪŋ/压倒性的/The response was overwhelming.
paradox/ˈpærədɑːks/悖论/It's a paradox that technology connects and isolates.
parallel/ˈpærəlel/平行的/The roads run parallel to each other.
parameter/pəˈræmɪtər/参数/You need to set the correct parameters.
partial/ˈpɑːrʃl/部分的；偏袒的/The report is partial and unfair.
passion/ˈpæʃn/激情/She has a passion for music.
patent/ˈpætnt/专利/He filed a patent for his invention.
pattern/ˈpætərn/模式/The pattern of behavior is common.
perceive/pərˈsiːv/感知/She perceived a change in his attitude.
percentage/pərˈsentɪdʒ/百分比/What percentage passed the exam?
perception/pərˈsepʃn/认知/People's perception of reality varies.
permanent/ˈpɜːrmənənt/永久的/He found a permanent job.
persist/pərˈsɪst/坚持/If you persist, you will succeed.
phenomenon/fɪˈnɑːmɪnən/现象/Global warming is a phenomenon.
philosophy/fɪˈlɑːsəfi/哲学/He studied philosophy at university.
pioneer/ˌpaɪəˈnɪr/先驱/She is a pioneer in biotechnology.
politics/ˈpɑːlətɪks/政治/He is interested in politics.
poll/poʊl/民意调查/A recent poll shows support for the plan.
portable/ˈpɔːrtəbl/便携的/This portable computer is convenient.
portion/ˈpɔːrʃn/部分/A large portion goes to education.
pose/poʊz/造成/The new policy poses a challenge.
postpone/poʊstˈpoʊn/推迟/The meeting has been postponed.
potential/pəˈtenʃl/潜力/He has the potential to succeed.
practical/ˈpræktɪkl/实际的/We need practical solutions.
precaution/prɪˈkɔːʃn/预防措施/We should take precautions.
precede/prɪˈsiːd/在…之前/The meeting was preceded by an introduction.
precious/ˈpreʃəs/珍贵的/Water is a precious resource.
precise/prɪˈsaɪs/精确的/Can you give a more precise answer?
